STAGE 1 - repository read and coupling trace.
GOAL: establish whether one connected pathway carries both the training-only successor-attraction weights and the Poincare operations, per check (a).
READ: tree root /fs04/ar57/wenyu/GeneRec/results/research/issue121/trees/round_20261028_233100_128/poincare-frechet-successor-codebook; files train_rqvae.py (595 lines), model/layers.py (342), model/frechet_poincare.py (217), model/model.py (94), model/utils.py (380, legacy, imported by nobody), model/__init__.py.
OBSERVED: The coupled path exists and is single:
 - train_rqvae.py:256-300 _build_successor_attraction (train parquet only, user->user consecutive pairs, self-transitions removed at 291-293, w=(indeg+1)/(n+2), np.clip 0.25..4, global mean-1 normalise);
 - train_rqvae.py:329-333 binds it into every level's FrechetCodebook as a buffer;
 - layers.py:140-149 curved branch of VQLayer.forward: point=exp_0(latent) (145), weights=weight_of(item_ids) (146), cost=Poincare distance to codebook (147), argmin (148), remember(point,index,weights) (149);
 - layers.py:166-170: commitment = Poincare_distance(point, code_book)**2 weighted by the SAME w in quant_loss = beta*(weights*commitment).mean() + mse(x, log_0(code).detach());
 - model/model.py:40-63 frechet_step_sums -> frechet_poincare.py:159-186 accumulate (log_at at 181, weighted per-slot tangent sum);
 - train_rqvae.py:441-449 DDP all_reduce of the sums then apply_frechet_codebook_step -> model.py:65-80 -> frechet_poincare.py:188-211 apply (exp_at at 203) -> layer.embed.weight.data.copy_ (model.py:80) -> next forward's argmin (layers.py:147-148) -> exported SID (train_rqvae.py:538-551).
REASONING: removing the weights (use_behaviour=False, frechet_poincare.py:138-139 returns uniform ones) changes accumulate/apply and the commitment; removing curvature (use_curvature=False, 145-157, 180-207) changes the metric in assignment, commitment and step. So both factors are inside one computation that ends in the exported SID. Also verified the exported indices come from the curved argmin (get_indices -> rq(..., item_ids=arange(N))).
OPEN: still to check numerics/dead terms (b) and DDP/launcher/export (c). No torch and no shell, so b is judged from code.
